    "userStatement": "sunbeam has some alignemnet problems where it starts etc and in what direcitons is avove or below the caster but this can be fixed in production / ensure sunbeam does not goes over the actual covered area looks good otherwise to me",
    "approvalScope": "Sunbeam artwork and Sunburst ground-coverage-v2 presentation approved. Sunbeam attachment, sorting and covered-area fixes remain mandatory production work. Approval is not runtime installation.",
    "requiredProductionWork": [
      "Anchor the launch to the actual animated casting hand for every direction and camera.",
      "Correct front/back and above/below caster occlusion and Y sorting.",
      "Keep all discharge geometry, sparks and visible beam extent within the authoritative covered volume/mask: 60 feet long, 5 feet wide, respecting backend clipping.",
      "Measure range from the gameplay origin; an offset hand socket must never extend the endpoint or shift the covered corridor.",
      "Check eight directions across four cameras, boundary recipients, an empty line and obstruction-clipped coverage."
    ],
    "sentToProduction": false,
    "productionInstalledByThisBatch": false,
    "coverageAudit": "authoring/coverage-audit.json",
